          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+gauge+theory"}> higher
            )
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+theory"} gauge theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fluxes"} fluxes
            through given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surfaces"} surfaces
            (or higher
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/submanifolds"} submanifolds
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/observables"} observables
            and hence have
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+brackets"} Poisson brackets
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+field+theory"} classical field theory
            To the extent that these induce non-trivial operator
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutators"} commutators
            in the corresponding
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heisenberg+uncertainty+principle"} Heisenberg uncertainty principle
          %p
            A subtlety here is that the usual
            = succeed "-methods" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phase+space"} phase space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+field+theories"} Lagrangian field theories
            directly provide these brackets only for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+forms"} differential forms
            which are the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+densities"} flux densities
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"} rational
            image of the fluxes, which in general may furthermore have
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsion+subgroup"} torsion
            = succeed "-components." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+group"} cohomology
          %p
            In plain
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electromagnetism"} electromagnetism
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+momentum"} canonical momentum
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+potential"} gauge potential
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is proportional (by constants to be ignored in the following) to the electric flux density
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⋆
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \star F
            (where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Faraday+tensor"} Faraday tensor
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+density"} flux density
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⋆
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \star
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hodge+star+operator"} Hodge star operator
            on the given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudo-Riemannian+manifold"} pseudo-Riemannian manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo ≡
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                    %mi dR
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \equiv \mathrm{d}_{dR} A
            with the electric flux density is a total derivative (cf. eg.
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "Yang-Mills+theory#BlaschkeGieres21"} Blaschke &amp; Gieres 2021 (5.5)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Φ
                    %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi_E
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Φ
                    %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi_B
            through given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientable+manifold"} orientable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+manifold"} closed
            surfaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_E
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_B
            %a{:href => "#FreedMooreSegal07b"} FMS07b (3.6)
            and Prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PoissonBracketBetweenElectricAndMagneticFluxes"}
            below):
          #eq:CommutingAbelianFluxes.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi Φ
                    %mi E
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi Φ
                    %mi B
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} }
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≡
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} {
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %msub
                      %mo ∫
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi S
                          %mi B
                    %mo ⋆
                    %mi F
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                      %msub
                        %mo ∫
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi S
                            %mi E
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} }
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo =
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mn 0
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\big\{
                  \\Phi_E
                  ,\,
                  \\Phi_B
                  \\big\}
                  \\;\equiv\;
                  \\Big\{
                  \\textstyle{\int}_{S_B} \star F
                  ,\,
                  \\textstyle{\int}_{S_E} F
                  \\Big\}
                  \\;=\;
                  0
                  \\,.
          %p
            The thrust of
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#FreedMooreSegal07a"} FMS 07a
            %a{:href => "#FreedMooreSegal07b"} 07b
            is the claim that this bracket becomes non-vanishing if torsion-components of the fluxes (through their enhancement to
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+differential+cohomology"} ordinary differential cohomology
            = succeed ";" do
              %a{:href => "#FreedMooreSegal07a"} FMS07a, Def. 1.29
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#FreedMooreSegal07b"} FMS07b (3.28)
          %p
            On the other hand, for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-abelian+group"} non-abelian
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+group"} gauge group
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#CattaneoPerez17"} Cattaneo &amp; Perez 2017
