            of the pairing and skew-symmetry of the Lie bracket).
          %p
            %br/
          %p
          #TheLieAlgebrasu2.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              In the case
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo =
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g} =
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/su%282%29"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔰𝔲
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{su}(2)
              equipped with its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Killing+form"} Killing form
              and with linear basis taken to be the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pauli+matrices"} Pauli matrices
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mi j
                            %mi k
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi ϵ
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mi j
                            %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_{i j k} = \epsilon_{i j k}
                  the
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Levi-Civita+symbol"} Levi-Civita symbol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi k
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mi j
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi δ
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mi j
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_{i j} = \delta_{i j}
                  the
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kronecker+delta"} Kronecker delta
            %p
              This is the case considered in
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#CattaneoPerez17"} Cattaneo &amp; Perez 2017
          %p
            %br/
          %h3#ThePoissonBracketOfCanonicalVariables The phase space of Yang-Mills theory
          %p
            We consider now such
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra-valued+differential+forms"} Lie algebra-valued differential forms
            on a given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth 3-manifold
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+surface"} Cauchy surface
            in a 3+1-dimensional
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
          %p
            On the space of
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:GaugePotential"} (3)
            and 2-forms
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinate+chart"} coordinate chart
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 3
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^3 \hookrightarrow X
            we may expand as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msubsup
                    %mi A
                    %mi a
                    %mi i
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mi a
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msub
                    %mi t
                    %mi u
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi E
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msubsup
                    %mi E
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mi b
                    %mi i
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mi a
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mi b
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msub
                    %mi t
                    %mi u
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  A
                  \\,=\,
                  A_a^i \, \mathrm{d}x^a \otimes t_u
                  \\,,
                  \\;\;\;\;
                  E \,=\,
                  E_{a b}^i \,
                  \\mathrm{d} x^a \wedge \mathrm{d} x^b \otimes t_u
                  \\,,
          %p
            we declare the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distribution"} distributional
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+bracket"} Poisson bracket
          #eq:ThePoissonBracketOnCanonicalCoordinates.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (19)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mtable{:columnalign => "left", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                    %mtr
                      %mtd
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} {
                        %msubsup
                          %mi E
                          %mrow
                            %mi a
                            %mi b
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %msubsup
                          %mi E
                          %mrow
                            %mi c
                            %mi d
                          %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ′
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} }
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo =
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mn 0
                    %mtr
                      %mtd
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} {
                        %msubsup
                          %mi A
                          %mi a
                          %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %msubsup
                          %mi A
                          %mi b
                          %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ′
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} }
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo =
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mn 0
                    %mtr
                      %mtd
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} {
                        %msubsup
                          %mi E
                          %mrow
                            %mi a
                            %mi b
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %msubsup
                          %mi A
                          %mi c
                          %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ′
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} }
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ≡
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %msup
                          %mi k
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mi j
                        %msub
                          %mi ϵ
                          %mrow
                            %mi a
                            %mi b
                            %mi c
                        %mi δ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi x
                        %mo ′
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{array}{l}
                  \\big\{ E^i_{a b}(x), E^j_{c d}(x') \big\}
                  \\;=\; 0
                  \\\
                  \\big\{ A^j_a(x), A^j_b(x') \big\}
                  \\;=\; 0
                  \\\
                  \\big\{ E^i_{a b}(x), A^j_c(x') \big\}
                  \\;\equiv\;
                  k^{ i j } \epsilon_{a b c} \delta(x,x')
                  \\end{array}
          %p
            together with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+class+constraint"} first class constraint
            that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covariant+derivative"} covariant derivative
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:CovariantDerivative"} (9)
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            vanishes:
          #eq:GaussLawConstraint.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (20)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                    %mi A
                  %mi E
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≈
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mn 0
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathrm{d}_A E \;\approx\; 0
                  \\,.
          %p
            This is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phase+space"} phase space
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"} Yang-Mills theory
            \&amp;lbrack;eg.
            = succeed ";" do
              %a{:href => "Yang-Mills+theory#FriedmanPapastamatiou83"} Friedman &amp; Papastamatiou 1983, §3
            = succeed "&rbrack;" do
              %a{:href => "Yang-Mills+theory#BassettoLazzizzeraSoldati84"} Bassetto, Lazzizzera &amp; Soldati 1984, §2
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+coordinate"} canonical coordinate
                being the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+potential"} gauge potential
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                in
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/temporal+gauge"} temporal gauge
            %li
              %p
                its
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+momentum"} canonical momentum
                being the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electric+field"} electric field
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+density"} flux density
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constrained+mechanics"} constraint
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:GaussLawConstraint"} (20)
                expressing the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gauss+law"} Gauss law
          %p
            %br/
          %p
            On this phase space, we are concerned with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/observables"} observables
            expressing electromagnetic flux through
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+manifold"} closed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/oriented+manifold"} oriented
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surface"} surface
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/submanifolds"} submanifolds
            (not necessarily
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+topological+space"} connected
          #eq:TheEmbeddedSurfaces.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (21)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mover
                    %mo ↪
                    %mphantom
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo −
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mi X
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  S \xhookrightarrow{\phantom{---}} X
                  \\,.
          %p
            Taken at face value, the linear such observables are the surface
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integration+of+differential+forms"} integrals
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+densities"} flux densities
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            against
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
          #eq:NaiveFluxObservables.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (22)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mtable{:columnalign => "center", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                    %mtr
                      %mtd
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Φ
                          %mi E
                          %mi α
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mover
                          %mo ≡
                          %mo ?
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %msub
                          %mo ∫
                          %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                        %mi α
                        %mo ,
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ,
                    %mtr
                      %mtd
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Φ
                          %mi B
                          %mi β
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mover
                          %mo ≡
                          %mo ?
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %msub
                          %mo ∫
                          %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                        %mi α
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi F
                          %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mtext for
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
